-- What the core 5th-level spells do, in a sentence or three of our own words. Shown
-- in place of the bare facts a spell's entry is built from (see Data/SpellSummaries.lua).
local _, ns = ...
local R = ns.Rules

R.SPELL_SUMMARIES = R.SPELL_SUMMARIES or {}
local S = R.SPELL_SUMMARIES

S["Animate Objects"] = "Loose objects within 120 feet, as many as your spellcasting modifier (a Large one counts as two, a Huge one as three), come alive and fight for you for up to a minute. They act right after your turn; a bonus action commands them. Their slam grows with each slot level above 5th."
S["Antilife Shell"] = "For up to an hour no creature except constructs and undead can pass or reach through a barrier 10 feet around you. Spells and ranged or reach attacks still cross it. It ends if you push it into a creature."
S["Awaken"] = "Takes 8 hours. A beast or plant of little mind that you touch gains an Intelligence of 10 and a language you know; a plant can also move and sense. It is charmed by you for 30 days, or until you or your allies harm it."
S["Banishing Smite"] = "Bonus action right after you hit with a weapon or unarmed strike: 5d10 extra force damage. If that leaves the target at 50 hit points or fewer, it must pass a Charisma save or be sent to a harmless pocket space, incapacitated, for up to a minute."
S["Bigby's Hand"] = "A Large hand of force appears within 120 feet for up to a minute. When you cast it and with a bonus action after, it moves 60 feet and punches (a melee spell attack for 5d8 force damage), shoves, grapples and crushes, or shields you from one creature. 2d8 more on the punch for each slot level above 5th."
S["Circle of Power"] = "For up to 10 minutes you and your allies within 30 feet of you have advantage on saves against spells and magic, and take no damage instead of half when you pass such a save."
S["Cloudkill"] = "Poison fog fills a 20-foot sphere within 120 feet for up to 10 minutes and drifts 10 feet away from you each turn. A creature in it when it appears, or that enters or ends its turn there, takes 5d8 poison damage, half on a successful Constitution save. 1d8 more for each slot level above 5th."
S["Commune"] = "Takes a minute. You ask a divine power up to three yes-or-no questions and receive true answers, or \"unclear\" where it doesn't know. Each further casting before a long rest has a growing chance of no answer."
S["Commune with Nature"] = "Takes a minute. You learn three facts of your choice about the land within 3 miles, or 300 feet underground: settlements, portals, water, a powerful otherworldly creature, or the commonest plants, minerals or beasts. It doesn't work in built-up places."
S["Cone of Cold"] = "A blast of cold in a 60-foot cone from you: 8d8 cold damage, half on a successful Constitution save. 1d8 more for each slot level above 5th."
S["Conjure Elemental"] = "A Large spirit of air, earth, fire or water appears within 60 feet for up to 10 minutes. A creature that enters its space or starts its turn within 5 feet must pass a Dexterity save or take 8d8 damage and be restrained; it saves again each turn, taking 4d8 on a failure. It holds one creature at a time. 1d8 more for each slot level above 5th."
S["Conjure Volley"] = "Spectral weapons rain down in a 40-foot radius within 150 feet: the creatures you choose take 8d8 force damage, half on a successful Dexterity save."
S["Contact Other Plane"] = "Takes a minute. You make a DC 15 Intelligence save. If you pass, a being from beyond answers up to five questions with a word each. If you fail, you take 6d6 psychic damage and are incapacitated until you finish a long rest."
S["Contagion"] = "A creature you touch that fails a Constitution save takes 11d8 necrotic damage and is poisoned, with disadvantage on saves with one ability you choose. It saves at the end of each of its turns: three successes end it, three failures make it last 7 days."
S["Creation"] = "Takes a minute. You make an object of plant or mineral matter you have seen, up to a 5-foot cube, within 30 feet. It lasts from a day for cloth or wood down to a minute for adamantine or mithral. 5 feet larger for each slot level above 5th."
S["Destructive Wave"] = "A shockwave 30 feet around you: the creatures you choose take 5d6 thunder and 5d6 radiant or necrotic damage and fall prone. A successful Constitution save halves the damage and keeps them standing."
S["Dispel Evil and Good"] = "For up to a minute celestials, elementals, fey, fiends and undead have disadvantage on attacks against you. You can end it early with an action: to free a creature you touch from their charm, fear or possession, or to send one within 5 feet home unless it passes a Charisma save."
S["Dominate Person"] = "A humanoid within 60 feet that fails a Wisdom save is charmed for up to a minute and obeys your mental commands. It saves again whenever it takes damage. Higher slots last longer: 10 minutes at 6th, an hour at 7th, 8 hours at 8th."
S["Dream"] = "Takes a minute. You or a willing creature you touch enters the dreams of a creature you know and can talk with it and shape the dream, for up to 8 hours. A nightmare instead: unless the sleeper passes a Wisdom save it gains nothing from its rest and takes 3d6 psychic damage on waking."
S["Flame Strike"] = "A column of fire, 10 feet in radius, strikes within 60 feet: 5d6 fire and 5d6 radiant damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. 1d6 more of each for each slot level above 5th."
S["Geas"] = "Takes a minute. A creature within 60 feet that understands you and fails a Wisdom save is charmed for 30 days and bound to a command. Acting against it deals 5d10 psychic damage, at most once a day. A year with a 7th or 8th-level slot; until removed with a 9th."
S["Greater Restoration"] = "Your touch removes one of these from a creature: a level of exhaustion, the charmed or petrified condition, a curse, a lowered ability score or a lowered hit point maximum."
S["Hallow"] = "Takes 24 hours. Ground up to 60 feet around a point you touch is warded until dispelled: the otherworldly creature types you pick can't enter it, nor charm, frighten or possess those inside. You add one extra effect, such as courage, daylight, silence or resistance to a damage type."
S["Hold Monster"] = "A creature within 90 feet that fails a Wisdom save is paralyzed for up to a minute. It saves again at the end of each of its turns. One more target for each slot level above 5th."
S["Insect Plague"] = "Locusts fill a 20-foot sphere within 300 feet for up to 10 minutes: lightly obscured, difficult terrain. A creature in it when it appears, or that enters or ends its turn there, takes 4d10 piercing damage, half on a successful Constitution save. 1d10 more for each slot level above 5th."
S["Jallarzi's Storm of Radiance"] = "A storm of light and thunder, 10 feet in radius, rages within 120 feet for up to a minute. Creatures inside are blinded and deafened and can't cast spells with spoken words. One in it when it appears, or that enters or ends its turn there, takes 2d10 radiant and 2d10 thunder damage, half on a successful Constitution save. 1d10 more of each for each slot level above 5th."
S["Legend Lore"] = "Takes 10 minutes. You name a famous person, place or object and the main lore about it comes to mind: accurate, but perhaps told in riddles. The more you already know, the more you learn."
S["Mass Cure Wounds"] = "Up to six creatures in a 30-foot sphere within 60 feet regain 5d8 hit points plus your spellcasting modifier. 1d8 more for each slot level above 5th."
S["Mislead"] = "You turn invisible and an illusory double takes your place for up to an hour. An action moves the double at twice your speed and makes it act and speak; you can see and hear through it. Attacking, dealing damage or casting ends the invisibility."
S["Modify Memory"] = "A creature within 30 feet that fails a Wisdom save is charmed and unaware for up to a minute while you rewrite its memory of an event in the last 24 hours, up to 10 minutes long. Damage breaks the spell. Higher slots reach further back: 7 days, 30 days, a year, any time."
S["Passwall"] = "A passage up to 5 feet wide, 8 feet tall and 20 feet deep opens in wood, plaster or stone within 30 feet for an hour. Anyone inside when it closes is pushed out safely."
S["Planar Binding"] = "Takes an hour. A celestial, elemental, fey or fiend that stays within 60 feet for the whole casting and fails a Charisma save must serve you for 24 hours, following your instructions as it understands them. Higher slots bind longer: 10, 30, 180 and 366 days."
S["Raise Dead"] = "Takes an hour. A creature you touch that has been dead for no more than 10 days returns with 1 hit point, cured of poison but without lost body parts. It has -4 to d20 rolls, easing by 1 with each long rest."
S["Rary's Telepathic Bond"] = "Up to eight willing creatures within 30 feet can speak mind to mind with each other for an hour, over any distance on the same plane and without a shared language."
S["Reincarnate"] = "Takes an hour. A humanoid dead for no more than 10 days, or a piece of one, that you touch returns to life in a new adult body of a random species, keeping its memories and abilities."
S["Scrying"] = "Takes 10 minutes. You watch and listen to a creature on your plane for up to 10 minutes through an invisible sensor, unless it passes a Wisdom save; the better you know it, the harder the save. You can watch a place you have seen instead."
S["Seeming"] = "The creatures you choose within 30 feet look different for 8 hours, bodies and gear, each as you decide. An unwilling one resists with a Charisma save. Touch gives it away, and an Investigation check against your spell save DC sees through it."
S["Steel Wind Strike"] = "You vanish and strike up to five creatures within 30 feet: a melee spell attack against each for 6d10 force damage; the sheet rolls all five. You then appear within 5 feet of one of them."
S["Summon Celestial"] = "A celestial spirit, an avenger or a defender, appears within 90 feet and fights for you for up to an hour, acting right after your turn on your spoken commands. A higher slot makes it stronger."
S["Summon Dragon"] = "A dragon spirit appears within 60 feet and fights for you for up to an hour, acting right after your turn on your spoken commands. A higher slot makes it stronger."
S["Swift Quiver"] = "Bonus action. For up to a minute, when you cast it and with a bonus action on later turns, you make two attacks with a weapon that shoots arrows or bolts. The spell supplies the ammunition."
S["Synaptic Static"] = "A psychic burst in a 20-foot sphere within 120 feet: 8d6 psychic damage, half on a successful Intelligence save. Those that fail also subtract 1d6 from attacks, checks and concentration saves for a minute, saving again at the end of each of their turns."
S["Telekinesis"] = "For up to 10 minutes, when you cast it and with an action after, you move a Huge or smaller creature or object within 60 feet up to 30 feet by thought. A creature resists with a Strength save and is restrained while held; an object in someone's grip is pulled away unless they pass one."
S["Teleportation Circle"] = "Takes a minute. You draw a circle within 10 feet that opens a portal, until the end of your next turn, to a permanent teleportation circle on your plane whose sigils you know."
S["Tree Stride"] = "For up to a minute you can step into a living tree your size or larger and out of another of the same kind within 500 feet, once each turn, for 5 feet of movement."
S["Wall of Force"] = "An invisible wall appears within 120 feet for up to 10 minutes: ten 10-foot panels, or a dome or globe up to 10 feet in radius. Nothing physical passes it, it is immune to all damage and can't be dispelled."
S["Wall of Stone"] = "A stone wall of ten 10-foot panels, 6 inches thick, rises within 120 feet and merges with nearby stone. Each panel can be broken. A creature about to be walled in can use its reaction and a Dexterity save to get out. Held for the full 10 minutes, it becomes permanent."
S["Yolande's Regal Presence"] = "Majesty surrounds you for 10 feet for up to a minute. A creature the aura reaches, or that enters it or ends its turn there, takes 4d6 psychic damage, falls prone and can be pushed 10 feet; a successful Wisdom save halves the damage and avoids the rest. Once per turn."
